Relevant columns, their usage & likely conditions  
• "refresh_date": locate the most‑recent data snapshot (MAX("refresh_date")).  
• "week": pick the latest week for that snapshot, then calculate the same week one year earlier (DATEADD(year,‑1,…)).  
• "rank": find the top‑ranked record (smallest value; usually 1 or MIN("rank")).  
• "term": the rising search term we ultimately want to display.  
• "percent_gain": optional for extra context when viewing results.  
• "dma_name"/"dma_id": optional when you want to see which U.S. DMA the search term belongs to.  

We will work inside the GOOGLE_TRENDS.GOOGLE_TRENDS.TOP_RISING_TERMS table.

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (LIMIT 20 rows each, all identifiers in double quotes) that progress from simple inspection to isolating the single record required by the task.

